ethod 1**\n\nFirst, we convert the percentage to a decimal:\n\n$$\n40%=40÷100=0.4\n$$\n\nApplying our formula, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{part} & =\\text{percentage}\\times \\text{whole} \\\\  & =40%\\times 35 \\\\  & =0.4\\times 35 \\\\  & =14\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $40%$ of $35$ is $14.$ So, $14$ children have black hair.\n\n**Method 2**\n\nFirst, we convert the percentage to a fraction:\n\n$$\n40%=\\frac{40}{100}=\\frac{40÷20}{100÷20}=\\frac{2}{5}\n$$\n\nApplying our formula, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{part} & =\\text{percentage}\\times \\text{whole} \\\\  & =40%\\times 35 \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{5}\\times 35 \\\\  & =2\\times \\frac{35}{5} \\\\  & =2\\times 7 \\\\  & =14\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $40%$ of $35$ is $14.$ So, $14$ children have black hair."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186442098 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186147593 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "3626bdd2-ec13-5d74-a570-ec65ba682723" :knowledge-point/title "Finding Part of a Number Given a Whole and a Percentage"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1a068b8c-d7ba-58f6-aef1-67ea1b268b8b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$2$ children" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186442028} {:answer/id #uuid "9cc33901-aced-5646-ba74-8266e301a847" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$6$ children" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186442061} {:answer/id #uuid "ad1724f0-67ed-5ad3-942a-da4b1e5cc278" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$5$ children" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186442068} {:answer/id #uuid "b186ff6e-a361-50ef-9788-4eabb33fa439" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$4$ children" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186442072} {:answer/id #uuid "e960dbae-8631-5175-ac7b-8cb63d220ab3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$3$ children" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186442080}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e960dbae-8631-5175-ac7b-8cb63d220ab3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$3$ children" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186442080} :answer-field/id #uuid "0377d3b7-b2f3-5abe-89ea-7dc3a661c4b1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186442084}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "52b2f721-25f8-5813-9d4e-57bac8db769b" :question/math-academy-id "q-61151" :question/problem "In Maria's class, there are $30$ children. Of this amount, $10%$ walk to school. How many children walk to school?" :question/worked-solution "To solve this problem, we can use the formula:\n\n$$\n\\text{part}=\\text{percentage}\\times \\text{whole}\n$$\n\nIn our case, the whole is the total number of children in Maria's class, which is $30.$ The percentage is $10%,$ and the part is the number of children who walk to school.\n\n**Method 1**\n\nFirst, we convert the percentage to a decimal:\n\n$$\n10%=10÷100=0.1\n$$\n\nApplying our formula, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{part} & =\\text{percentage}\\times \\text{whole} \\\\  & =10%\\times 30 \\\\  & =0.1\\times 30 \\\\  & =3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $10%$ of $30$ is $3.$ Thus, $3$ children walk to school.\n\n**Method 2**\n\nFirst, we convert the percentage to a fraction:\n\n$$\n10%=\\frac{10}{100}=\\frac{10÷10}{100÷10}=\\frac{1}{10}\n$$\n\nApplying our formula, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{part} & =\\text{percentage}\\times \\text{whole} \\\\  & =10%\\times 30 \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{10}\\times 30 \\\\  & =\\frac{30}{10} \\\\  & =3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $10%$ of $30$ is $3.$ Thus, $3$ children walk to school."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186442100 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186147593 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "3626bdd2-ec13-5d74-a570-ec65ba682723" :knowledge-point/title "Finding Part of a Number Given a Whole and a Percentage"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "375b9c30-c252-598c-80f0-b9aa4d93803c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$14$ grapes" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186442033} {:answer/id #uuid "44d8e748-b602-5fa9-95ca-8c3d9b2ac389" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$16$ grapes" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186442036} {:answer/id #uuid "5bed1096-653c-5c18-8f32-375f32024b35" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$12$ grapes" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186442043} {:answer/id #uuid "a0aa0a0a-e9bf-512c-8870-61088113d83b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$15$ grapes" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186442063} {:answer/id #uuid "a581cf6e-89b6-5ab2-b324-834385f78789" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$18$ grapes" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186442065}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "375b9c30-c252-598c-80f0-b9aa4d93803c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$14$ grapes" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186442033} :answer-field/id #uuid "ceb325ac-a50b-51e2-bf5d-2c9c5d43b7fb" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186442092}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "5a809928-75f9-5540-949c-59cd2e66a5d3" :question/math-academy-id "q-61163" :question/problem "A bunch of grapes contained $50$ grapes. Serena eats $28%$ of them. How many grapes did Serena eat?" :question/worked-solution "To solve this problem, we can use the formula:\n\n$$\n\\text{part}=\\text{percentage}\\times \\text{whole}\n$$\n\nIn our case, the whole is the total number of grapes, which is $50$ grapes. The percentage is $28%,$ and the part is the number of grapes Serena ate.\n\n**Method 1**\n\nFirst, we convert the percentage to a decimal:\n\n$$\n28%=28÷100=0.28\n$$\n\nApplying our formula, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{part} & =\\text{percentage}\\times \\text{whole} \\\\  & =28%\\times 50 \\\\  & =0.28\\times 50 \\\\  & =14\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $28%$ of $50$ is $14.$ Thus, Serena ate $14$ grapes.\n\n**Method 2**\n\nFirst, we convert the percentage to a fraction:\n\n$$\n28%=\\frac{28}{100}=\\frac{28÷4}{100÷4}=\\frac{7}{25}\n$$\n\nApplying our formula, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{part} & =\\text{percentage}\\times \\text{whole} \\\\  & =28%\\times 50 \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{25}\\times 50 \\\\  & =7\\times \\frac{50}{25} \\\\  & =7\\times 2 \\\\  & =14\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $28%$ of $50$ is $14.$ Thus, Serena ate $14$ grapes."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186147871 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186147594 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "163d387b-3fd7-5f95-8245-5fb0184b371b" :knowledge-point/title "Finding Part of a Number Given a Whole and a Decimal Percentage"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c1f2eafc-911f-5f49-837b-aa3afc5a8973" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$$354$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186144981} {:answer/id #uuid "ef182a04-7dc6-578c-a576-01bfe5d27e45" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$$328$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186144982} {:answer/id #uuid "38d78784-9f89-56ca-9107-9e18be3b6b4f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$$320$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186144983} {:answer/id #uuid "648df517-6a96-5b5f-8a09-7a5f9c7c59eb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$$344$" :db/id #edb/ref 17