 & =22.4\\times 15 \\\\  & =336\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $22.4%$ of $1,500$ is $336.$ Thus, Margaret plans to spend $$336.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186442096 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186147594 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "163d387b-3fd7-5f95-8245-5fb0184b371b" :knowledge-point/title "Finding Part of a Number Given a Whole and a Decimal Percentage"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1899873a-5db0-554d-b2e9-82786157312c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "18" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186442027} {:answer/id #uuid "58a273ff-8c5d-50e1-a6a6-6b8cf66b4cdc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186442040} {:answer/id #uuid "6a756c6a-2cbc-593b-81c7-a68c8d67e96f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "15" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186442046} {:answer/id #uuid "70c024ff-5275-5181-b64b-e8a91a01b5f2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186442049} {:answer/id #uuid "75375067-fe0b-50ed-bfbd-eacda15e99c3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186442051}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6a756c6a-2cbc-593b-81c7-a68c8d67e96f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "15" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186442046} :answer-field/id #uuid "d042f82c-4cb1-56b8-b08d-5af028f1c43a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186442093}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "37153dd3-f5a5-5cb4-89d6-f95a95fd428d" :question/math-academy-id "q-61179" :question/problem "A party-planning company decorated a room with $200$ balloons. Of this amount, $7.5%$ of the balloons are white. How many white balloons are there?" :question/worked-solution "To solve this problem, we can use the formula:\n\n$$\n\\text{part}=\\text{percentage}\\times \\text{whole}\n$$\n\nIn our case, the whole is the number of balloons in the room, which is $200.$ The percentage is $7.5%,$ and the part is the number of white balloons.\n\n**Method 1**\n\nFirst, we convert the percentage to a decimal:\n\n$$\n7.5%=7.5÷100=0.075\n$$\n\nApplying our formula, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{part} & =\\text{percentage}\\times \\text{whole} \\\\  & =7.5%\\times 200 \\\\  & =0.075\\times 200 \\\\  & =15\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $7.5%$ of $200$ is $15.$ Thus, there are $15$ white balloons.\n\n**Method 2**\n\nFirst, we convert the percentage to a fraction:\n\n$$\n7.5%=\\frac{7.5}{100}\n$$\n\nApplying our formula, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{part} & =\\text{percentage}\\times \\text{whole} \\\\  & =7.5%\\times 200 \\\\  & =\\frac{7.5}{100}\\times 200 \\\\  & =7.5\\times \\frac{200}{100} \\\\  & =7.5\\times 2 \\\\  & =15\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $7.5%$ of $200$ is $15.$ Thus, there are $15$ white balloons."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186442101 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186147595 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "176069e4-4aa3-58cd-a04e-a70e7e5da960" :knowledge-point/title "Finding Part of a Number Given a Whole and a Percentage Greater Than 100%"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2622fd39-9743-578c-91cc-ca0821693de4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$$12,800$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186442030} {:answer/id #uuid "604a37eb-87cf-55a2-95bd-79746423730e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$$14,000$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186442045} {:answer/id #uuid "783f2ae0-2680-54b7-8c66-654710686a80" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 1759218604